{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788350814,"nonce":"ZGQ+3/dpX6gKxFXd1RyqL2K++/I=","title":"**Promoted from a comment on `d2e1229`.** Related to `5cb1f9f` but a separate gap.","message":"Colony start has an unwritten step: **the colony must be NAMED.** It does not fall due at colony start — it falls due days later, well after the colony-start checklist section is logged complete. In run `m1-20260901` it arrived at tick ~255,000 as `Dialog_NamePlayerFactionAndSettlement`, which is `forcePause` and `absorbsInput`, so every `advance` halted on it. `dialog-dismiss` removed the window and the game raised it again 1,000 ticks later, forever. Evan typed the name by hand — human input beyond watching, recorded as an invariant breach in the run report.\n\n`5cb1f9f` covers **answering** the dialog. This issue covers the fact that **nothing says it is coming or that it is outstanding.** An agent that knew a naming step was pending would recognise the halt instead of meeting an unrecognised window class mid-run.\n\n\nNothing in the mod reads the player faction's naming state. There is no `HasName` read, no settlement-name read, nothing in `digest.site` or `status`. Grep confirms it: the only `settlement` references in the source are `TradeVerbs` and `QuestVerbs` ruling world settlements out of scope.\n\n\n1. The observation surface publishes whether the colony naming step is outstanding — the player faction and its settlement each carrying a game-generated placeholder rather than a chosen name — as a boolean plus the current values, so an agent can see it pending before the dialog force-pauses the game. Establish against the decompiled source what the game itself tests before raising the dialog, and cite the member; do not infer it from the name string.\n2. `checklists/triggered.md` gains the naming step as an act-keyed item, and the colony-start section in `PLAY-LOOP.md` states that the section is **not** complete when it is logged complete — a named step falls due days later. This is the actual lesson: a checklist section that closes before its work is finished will hide that work forever.\n3. `accept/\u003cid\u003e-colony-naming.py` on a bench: assert the pending state reads true on a fresh colony, assert it reads false once named.\n\n\nIf the game's own trigger for the dialog turns out not to be a readable predicate — if it is scheduled rather than derived from state — then the observability half is not cleanly specifiable and should be parked with that finding written out. The `triggered.md` and `PLAY-LOOP.md` half stands on its own and ships regardless: an agent told to expect a naming prompt days into the run is materially better off than one that meets it cold.","files":null}]}